---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import { HeroGraphic, Architecture, Capability } from '../components/Foundation.jsx';
import LogoStrip from '../components/LogoStrip.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
---
<Site title="Choose and tune LLM inference with evidence">
  <section class="hero section"><div class="hero-copy"><h1>Better inference.<br/>Backed by<br/><em>evidence.</em></h1><p>Choose models with context. Run workloads remotely. Find the serving configurations that fit your throughput and latency needs.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="primary-button" href="/architecture">Explore the technology <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="hero-secondary" href="/demo">Enter the interactive lab ↗</a></div><div class="hero-proof"><span class="proof-icon">✓</span>Model research → execution → inference optimization</div></div><HeroGraphic client:load /></section>
  <LogoStrip />
  <section class="section editorial-section" data-reveal><div><h2>A model choice is<br/>only the beginning.</h2><p class="lede">A model’s reputation doesn’t tell you how it will serve your workload.</p></div><div><p>Revision, serving engine, GPU configuration, and request patterns shape the measurements. Infiro connects model research to execution and configuration search, keeping that context attached.</p><div class="context-chain"><span>Model revision</span><b>+</b><span>Serving settings</span><b>+</b><span>Workload</span><b>→</b><span class="accent-text">Evidence</span></div></div></section>
  <Architecture client:visible />
  <section class="section capability-grid" data-reveal><article><h3>Research with context.</h3><p>Nemotron-assisted assessment brings model metadata and sourced research into the selection process.</p><a href="/technology#research">Inspect the research workflow →</a></article><article><h3>Execute remotely.</h3><p>Nebius jobs run validation and optimization workloads through their existing orchestration paths.</p><a href="/technology#execution">Understand execution boundaries →</a></article><article><h3>Compare the tradeoffs.</h3><p>Fixed workloads, explicit objectives, and Pareto analysis make serving configurations easier to assess.</p><a href="/demo/pareto">Explore throughput and latency →</a></article></section>
  <Capability client:visible />
  <section class="section demo-preview" data-reveal><div><h2>Watch a search<br/><em>learn where to look.</em></h2><p>Step through actual TPE, Gaussian-process, and random sampler traces on the same synthetic objective. Change the seed. Inspect every observation.</p><a class="primary-button" href="/demo/search">Open the search playground <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="small muted">Offline simulations. Real algorithms. No GPU inference.</p></div><a class="simulation-teaser" href="/demo/search" aria-label="Explore the optimization playground"><svg viewBox="0 0 440 290" role="img" aria-label="Conceptual search contour illustration"><g fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)">{Array.from({length:12},(_,i)=><ellipse cx="220" cy="145" rx={18+i*15} ry={10+i*8} transform="rotate(-25 220 145)" opacity={.9-i*.065}/>)}</g>{Array.from({length:18},(_,i)=><circle cx={65+(i*61)%310} cy={50+(i*43)%190} r="3" fill="#6d9daf"/>)}<circle cx="220" cy="145" r="6" fill="var(--accent)"/></svg><span>Explore → observe → refine <b>Open lab ↗</b></span></a></section>
  <section class="section evidence-banner" data-reveal><div><h2>Measurements need context.</h2><p>We publish inference comparisons only when model revision, hardware, runtime, and workload can be traced. Current public examples are explicitly simulated.</p></div><div><a href="/benchmarks">Explore the benchmark interface →</a><a href="/methodology">Read the publication criteria →</a></div></section>
  <Callout />
</Site>
